        "summary": {
            "title": "What you have learnt",
            "points": [
                {
                    "text": "Density is the mass of each cm³. 8 g/cm³ means 8 g in each cm³."
                },
                {
                    "text": "Mass = density × volume. Density = mass ÷ volume. Volume = mass ÷ density."
                },
                {
                    "text": "The unit gives you the triangle: g/cm³ is grams ÷ cm³, so mass goes on top."
                },
                {
                    "text": "Make the units match: change kg to grams first (× 1000)."
                },
                {
                    "text": "Pressure is the force on each m²: pressure = force ÷ area. Same force on a bigger area means less pressure."
                }
            ]
        }
    },
